@russremboldt8006 here's the thing; they *do* consume fossil fuels to make. However, they produce green energy that doesn't pollute the planet, which over the lifetime of the panel far exceeds the amount used to create it. 

I really don't get why people are against green energy. For basic survival, we're eventually going to have to make the switch, and it's more profitable long term (like two decades long term, even). It's a far better investment than fossil fuels, which by nature are not renewable and therefore inefficient in creating and maintaining jobs. 

Economically, it makes sense to switch to green energy.
